Package: Proximum
Title: Statistical Analysis of Ensemble Proximity Matrices
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Agostino",
           family = "Gnasso",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "agostino.gnasso@unina.it",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8046-3923"))
Description: Treats the proximity matrices produced by tree ensembles as
    first-class statistical objects rather than as model by-products.
    Provides a unified extractor across ensemble engines, in-bag and
    out-of-bag definitions, transformations to dissimilarities with metric
    diagnostics, corrections that make an indefinite proximity usable as a
    kernel, and permutation inference for comparing two proximity matrices.
    Bootstrap stability assessment, approximations for large samples and
    dedicated visualisations are planned and not yet implemented; the
    functions that will provide them raise an error naming the release they
    are scheduled for.
